  "body": "1) Should the following form submit?\n\n```\n<form>\n  <input type=\"radio\" name=\"foo\" value=\"1\" required checked disabled>\n  <input type=\"radio\" name=\"foo\" value=\"2\" required>\n</form>\n```\n\n2) What about the same example, but without the `checked` attribute?\n\nFrom the spec:\n\"Suffering from being missing: When a control has no value but has a required attribute (input required, textarea required); or, in the case of an element in a radio button group, any of the other elements in the group has a required attribute; or, for select elements, none of the option elements have their selectedness set (select required).\"\n\nSo my question is: what is the value of a radio button group? Is it the value that would be sent on form submission? If so, neither examples should pass validations. Firefox & Chrome seem content in submitting the form above, even though no value for `foo` is sent. Without the `checked` attribute, both will browsers will show a validation error.\n\nShouldn't both cases be treated the same way, i.e. checked but disabled radio/checkboxes should be ignored when considering if a group passes constraint validations? Otherwise, is there some other definition of what the value of a radio group?\n",
